window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f3a0216fc3d2956b"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"_1\">计算机活动历史</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取对应的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 macOS 版 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，ChatGPT Pro、Business 和 Enterprise 用户的“计算机活动历史”功能<strong>默认关闭</strong>。Pro 用户可以自行选择开启。对于 Business 和 Enterprise 工作区，管理员必须先明确授予访问权限，成员之后才能选择开启。此功能还需要启用<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>，并且不能通过 API 密钥或 Amazon Bedrock 使用。该功能仅在受支持的地区提供，包括欧洲经济区（EEA）、瑞士和英国。</p> <p>“计算机活动历史”会将你在应用和网站中的活动整理成记忆和时间线，供 ChatGPT 和 Codex 参考。你可以用自然语言询问近期工作、接着之前的进度继续、了解自己的工作模式，也可以将重复的流程转化为技能或自动化任务。</p> <p>只有在你主动选择开启后，才会开始记录历史。你可以控制哪些应用和网站提供活动信息，也可以通过 macOS 菜单栏查看或暂停收集，并随时检查或删除历史记录。</p> <p>“计算机活动历史”取代了早期的 Chronicle 研究预览版，但这是重新构建的系统，并非仅仅改名。它会使用交互事件，以及 macOS 辅助功能提供的文本和其他上下文，生成供你检查和删除的摘要。历史记录不包含屏幕截图，也不会录制音频；隐私浏览模式下的网页活动绝不会被纳入。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：计算机活动历史时间线，展示活动摘要、提供数据的应用，以及建议的技能和自动化任务</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"_2\">计算机活动历史能帮你做什么</h2> <p>“计算机活动历史”会将近期活动作为上下文。如果某个文件、Slack 对话、Google 文档或其他来源更适合完成任务，ChatGPT 和 Codex 可以先通过历史记录找到该来源，再直接读取它。</p> <section> <h3 id=\"_3\">接着之前的进度继续</h3> <p>不必重新回想当时打开了哪些应用和文档、下一步要做什么；直接询问休息前正在做的工作即可。</p> <p class=\"notice\">原网页此处包含交互演示，请通过“查看官方来源”联网查看。</p> </section> <section> <h3 id=\"_4\">查找近期工作</h3> <p>像平常回忆那样描述某个文档、对话或任务。“计算机活动历史”可以利用活动时间线识别你所指的来源。</p> <p class=\"notice\">原网页此处包含交互演示，请通过“查看官方来源”联网查看。</p> </section> <section> <h3 id=\"_5\">重用工作流程</h3> <p>当“计算机活动历史”发现可重复执行的工作时，时间线条目可能会建议创建技能或自动化任务。你可以先检查建议，再让 Codex 根据记录的工作流程创建它。</p> <p class=\"notice\">原网页此处包含交互演示，请通过“查看官方来源”联网查看。</p> </section> <h2 id=\"_6\">计算机活动历史的工作方式</h2> <p>“计算机活动历史”会从获准的应用和网站收集交互事件流。事件可能包括点击、键入、键盘快捷键、应用切换，以及 macOS 通过辅助功能系统提供的上下文。它会定期将这些事件整理成文本摘要和本地记忆文件。</p> <p>“计算机活动历史”不会在历史记录中包含屏幕截图，也不会录制麦克风输入或系统音频。隐私浏览模式下的网页活动绝不会被纳入。</p> <p>在 <strong>设置 &gt; 计算机活动历史 &gt; 历史记录</strong> 中，时间线会按日期和时间归类摘要。每个条目可能显示：</p> <ul> <li>活动标题和文字摘要。</li> <li>为摘要提供信息的应用。</li> <li>ChatGPT 发现可重复工作时建议的技能或自动化任务。</li> <li>在 Finder 中显示记忆文件或删除该条目的操作。</li> </ul> <p>选择 <strong>询问历史记录</strong>，即可开始与“计算机活动历史”聊天；也可以使用以下提示词：</p> <ul> <li>“我上次休息之前在做什么？”</li> <li>“今天早些时候我找的那份提案文档在哪里？”</li> <li>“列出我今天做过的任务及其状态。”</li> <li>“帮我整理一份昨天工作内容的摘要，供站会使用。”</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_7\">权限与访问</h2> <p>“计算机活动历史”分别控制工作区访问权限、个人选择加入、记忆，以及哪些应用或网站会纳入历史记录：</p> <ul> <li><strong>工作区访问：</strong> Business 和 Enterprise 工作区中的“计算机活动历史”默认关闭，管理员明确授予访问权限前不可使用。Enterprise 管理员可以在<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>工作区设置（Workspace Settings）&gt; 权限与角色（Permissions &amp; roles）</strong>（需联网）</a>中选择<strong>启用计算机活动历史（Enable Computer History）</strong>，向合适的工作区角色授予访问权限。</li> <li><strong>个人选择加入：</strong> 授予工作区访问权限，只代表成员可以选择开启“计算机活动历史”，并不会自动替任何人开启。每个人都必须单独选择加入，ChatGPT Pro 用户也不例外。</li> <li><strong>记忆：</strong> “计算机活动历史”也需要<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>。使用 <code>/memories</code> 控制某次聊天是否可以使用本地记忆，或为后续记忆提供内容。</li> <li><strong>应用和网站：</strong> 应用和网站权限决定哪些来源可以提供交互事件。你可以只允许特定来源，也可以排除不希望纳入的应用和网站 URL。</li> </ul> <p>如果你的工作区角色没有访问权限，仅更改本地设置无法启用“计算机活动历史”。</p> <h2 id=\"_8\">开启计算机活动历史</h2> <p>“计算机活动历史”默认关闭。如果你使用 Business 或 Enterprise 工作区，请先让管理员授予访问权限，再自行开启。管理员批准并不代表你已经选择加入。</p> <ol> <li>在 macOS 上打开 ChatGPT 桌面应用。</li> <li>打开“设置”（Settings），在 <strong>Integrations（集成）</strong> 下选择 <strong>Computer history（计算机活动历史）</strong>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Turn on（开启）</strong>，并阅读有关隐私、权限和本地存储的信息。</li> <li>如果系统提示，请开启 <strong>Memories（记忆）</strong>。“计算机活动历史”需要记忆功能，才能在不同聊天和任务之间使用活动上下文。</li> <li>选择哪些应用和网站可以为历史记录提供信息，然后按提示授予 macOS 所需权限。</li> </ol> <p>“计算机活动历史”不需要“屏幕录制”权限。如果看不到该设置，请确认你的套餐支持此功能；如果适用，也请确认工作区管理员已启用此功能。</p> <h2 id=\"_9\">控制纳入哪些内容</h2> <p>你可以控制哪些应用和网站会为未来的历史记录提供信息，以及“计算机活动历史”当前是否正在收集交互事件。</p> <h3 id=\"_10\">选择应用和网站</h3> <p>在 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Computer history（计算机活动历史）&gt; Permissions（权限）</strong> 中，选择“计算机活动历史”可以纳入哪些应用和网站：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Exclude these apps（排除这些应用）</strong>和 <strong>Exclude these websites（排除这些网站）</strong>会阻止你指定的应用或 URL，同时允许其他受支持的来源。</li> <li><strong>Include only these apps（仅纳入这些应用）</strong>和 <strong>Include only these websites（仅纳入这些网站）</strong>只允许你明确选择的来源。</li> </ul> <p>你也可以在历史时间线条目中选择某个应用图标，将该应用从今后的历史记录中排除。之后仍可重新纳入。</p> <p>隐私浏览模式下的网页活动绝不会被纳入。更改应用或网站权限只会影响今后的历史记录。若要移除已有条目，请删除或清除它们。</p> <h3 id=\"_11\">暂停、恢复或停止收集</h3> <p>使用“计算机活动历史”设置或 macOS 菜单栏，控制此功能何时收集活动：</p> <ul> <li>在 macOS 菜单栏中选择 ChatGPT 图标，然后展开 Computer History 菜单，查看它收集哪些活动并使用相关控制项。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Pause（暂停）</strong>，停止收集新的交互事件；准备好继续时，选择 <strong>Resume（恢复）</strong>。</li> <li>关闭“计算机活动历史”，即可停止今后的活动收集。</li> </ul> <p>“计算机活动历史”可能会收集通信应用和网站中的交互事件。除非事先获得他人明确同意，否则与他人交流时请关闭该功能。对于包含敏感健康、财务或个人信息的应用，也可以考虑暂停收集或将其排除。</p> <p>暂停“计算机活动历史”后，不会再收集新的交互事件；但正在处理的先前事件摘要可能会继续生成，直到处理完成。</p> <h2 id=\"_12\">查看和清除历史记录</h2> <p>打开 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Computer history（计算机活动历史）&gt; History（历史记录）</strong>，检查“计算机活动历史”生成的摘要。你可以在 Finder 中显示某个摘要对应的本地记忆文件、删除单个时间线条目，或清除最近 10 分钟、最近 1 小时、最近 1 天的记录以及全部历史记录。macOS 菜单栏还可以清除最近使用的某个应用的上一会话记录。</p> <p>清除历史记录会删除相关交互事件，以及由这些事件创建的记忆。此操作无法撤销。</p> <h2 id=\"_13\">隐私与本地存储</h2> <p>“计算机活动历史”会在 Mac 上临时存储交互事件流，以便 ChatGPT 和 Codex 生成记忆并整理建议的工作流程。事件流可能包含点击、键入等活动，以及 macOS 辅助功能所提供的文本和其他上下文。“计算机活动历史”不会在历史记录中包含屏幕截图，也不会录制麦克风输入或系统音频。隐私浏览模式下的网页活动绝不会被纳入。</p> <p>临时事件文件最多保留 48 小时。生成的记忆文件会一直保留在你的文件系统中，直到你将其删除或清除；你也可以从“历史记录”时间线中打开这些文件所在的位置。</p> <h3 id=\"_14\">计算机活动历史会在哪里存储我的数据？</h3> <p>“计算机活动历史”会在 Mac 上临时保存交互事件。事件文件存放在 ChatGPT 的<a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/protecting-local-app-data-using-containers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">应用组（App Group）（需联网）</a>中，与其他应用隔离，未经明确授权，其他应用无法访问这些文件。ChatGPT 和 Codex 会在 48 小时后删除事件文件。</p> <p>“计算机活动历史”会像 Codex 一样生成本地记忆：可供你阅读和修改的纯文本 Markdown 文件。这些文件保存在 <code>$CODEX_HOME/memories/extensions/skysight/</code> 下；该路径通常对应 <code>~/.codex/memories/extensions/skysight/</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>提示（<code>danger</code>）</strong>: 计算机活动历史文件可能包含敏感信息。计算机活动历史不会对这些文件加密；以你的 macOS 用户身份运行的其他程序也可能访问它们。请保护好 Mac 账户，并排除不希望纳入记录的来源。</p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"openai\">哪些数据会与 OpenAI 共享？</h3> <p>“计算机活动历史”会先在本地捕获交互事件，然后定期启动一个临时 Codex 会话，使其能够访问交互事件流，并将你的活动整理成记忆。</p> <p>OpenAI 会在服务器上处理临时事件文件以生成记忆，然后将记忆存储在你的 Mac 本地。除非法律要求，OpenAI 不会在处理完成后保留这些事件文件，也不会将其用于训练。</p> <p>在之后的聊天中，如果 ChatGPT 或 Codex 使用某条记忆，相关记忆内容和交互事件可能会作为上下文提供。若你的 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/7730893-data-controls-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 数据控制设置（需联网）</a>允许，这些聊天内容可能会用于改进 OpenAI 模型。记忆也遵循<a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc?anchor=control-memories-per-chat\">与其他 Codex 记忆相同的单聊天控制规则</a>。</p> <h3 id=\"_15\">提示词注入风险</h3> <p>“计算机活动历史”会增加应用和网站内容导致提示词注入的风险。例如，如果你访问了包含恶意指令的网站，ChatGPT 或 Codex 可能会遵循这些指令。</p> <h2 id=\"_16\">词元用量</h2> <p>“计算机活动历史”在汇总活动并创建记忆时会使用词元。</p> <h2 id=\"_17\">故障排查</h2> <p>如果“计算机活动历史”已开放给你使用，但无法启动：</p> <ol> <li>确认 <strong>Memories（记忆）</strong> 已开启。</li> <li>打开 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Computer history（计算机活动历史）</strong>，根据页面显示的状态选择 <strong>Finish setup（完成设置）</strong>、<strong>Resume（恢复）</strong> 或 <strong>Try again（重试）</strong>。</li> <li>如果设置仍不可用，请退出并重新打开 ChatGPT 桌面应用。</li> </ol>","en":"<h1 id=\"computer-history\">Computer History</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Computer History is <strong>off by default</strong> for ChatGPT Pro, Business, and Enterprise users in the ChatGPT desktop app on macOS. Pro users can choose to turn it on. For Business and Enterprise workspaces, an administrator must explicitly grant access before each member can choose to turn it on. Computer History also requires <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memories</a> and is not available with an API key or Amazon Bedrock. It's available in supported regions, including the European Economic Area (EEA), Switzerland, and the United Kingdom.</p> <p>Computer History turns your activity across apps and websites into memories and a timeline that ChatGPT and Codex can reference. You can ask natural questions about recent work, pick up where you left off, understand patterns in how you work, and turn repeated workflows into skills or automations.</p> <p>Your history starts only after you choose to turn it on. You control which apps and websites contribute, can see and pause collection from the macOS menu bar, and can inspect or delete your history at any time.</p> <p>Computer History replaces the earlier Chronicle research preview, but it is a rebuilt system rather than a rename. It uses interaction events, along with text and other context available through macOS accessibility features, to create summaries you can review and delete. It does not include screenshots in your history or record audio, and private-mode web browsing activity is never included.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Computer History timeline showing activity summaries, contributing apps, and suggested skills and automations</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"how-computer-history-helps\">How Computer History helps</h2> <p>Computer History supplies recent activity as context. When a file, Slack conversation, Google Doc, or another source is better for the task, ChatGPT and Codex can use the history to identify that source and then read it directly.</p> <section> <h3 id=\"pick-up-where-you-left-off\">Pick up where you left off</h3> <p>Ask what you were doing before a break without reconstructing every open app, document, and next step.</p> <p class=\"notice\">This part of the official page contains an interactive demo. Open the official source online to view it.</p> </section> <section> <h3 id=\"find-recent-work\">Find recent work</h3> <p>Refer to a document, conversation, or task the way you remember it. Computer History can use the activity timeline to identify the source you mean.</p> <p class=\"notice\">This part of the official page contains an interactive demo. Open the official source online to view it.</p> </section> <section> <h3 id=\"reuse-workflows\">Reuse workflows</h3> <p>When Computer History notices repeatable work, a timeline entry can suggest a skill or automation. Review the suggestion, then ask Codex to create it from the recorded workflow.</p> <p class=\"notice\">This part of the official page contains an interactive demo. Open the official source online to view it.</p> </section> <h2 id=\"how-computer-history-works\">How Computer History works</h2> <p>Computer History creates an interaction-event stream from allowed apps and websites. Events can include clicks, typing, keyboard shortcuts, app switches, and context that macOS exposes through its accessibility system. Computer History periodically turns these events into text summaries and local memory files.</p> <p>Computer History does not include screenshots in your history or record microphone input or system audio. Private-mode web browsing activity is never included.</p> <p>In <strong>Settings &gt; Computer history &gt; History</strong>, the timeline groups summaries by day and time. Each item can show:</p> <ul> <li>A title and text summary of the activity.</li> <li>The apps that contributed to the summary.</li> <li>A suggested skill or automation when ChatGPT identifies repeatable work.</li> <li>Actions to reveal the memory file in Finder or delete the item.</li> </ul> <p>Select <strong>Ask about your history</strong> to start a chat with Computer History, or use prompts such as:</p> <ul> <li>“What was I working on before my last break?”</li> <li>“Where can I find the proposal document I was looking for earlier today?”</li> <li>“Give me a list of tasks I’ve worked on today and their status.”</li> <li>“Prepare a summary of what I did yesterday for standup.”</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"permissions-and-access\">Permissions and access</h2> <p>Computer History uses separate controls for workspace access, personal opt-in, memories, and the apps or websites included in your history:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Workspace access:</strong> Computer History is off by default in Business and Enterprise workspaces and is unavailable until an administrator explicitly grants access. Enterprise administrators can use <strong>Enable Computer History</strong> in <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/admin/settings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Workspace Settings &gt; Permissions &amp; roles</strong> (online)</a> to grant access to the appropriate workspace roles.</li> <li><strong>Personal opt-in:</strong> Granting workspace access only lets a member choose to turn on Computer History. It does not turn on the feature for anyone. Each person must opt in individually, including ChatGPT Pro users.</li> <li><strong>Memories:</strong> Computer History also requires <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memories</a>. Use <code>/memories</code> to control whether an individual chat can use local memories or contribute to future memories.</li> <li><strong>Apps and websites:</strong> Your app and website permissions determine which sources can contribute interaction events. You can allow only specific sources or exclude apps and website URLs you do not want included.</li> </ul> <p>If your workspace role does not have access, changing local settings cannot enable Computer History.</p> <h2 id=\"turn-on-computer-history\">Turn on Computer History</h2> <p>Computer History is off by default. If you use a Business or Enterprise workspace, ask your administrator to grant you access before turning it on. Administrator approval does not opt you in.</p> <ol> <li>Open the ChatGPT desktop app on macOS.</li> <li>In Settings, under <strong>Integrations</strong>, select <strong>Computer history</strong>.</li> <li>Select <strong>Turn on</strong> and review the privacy, permissions, and local-storage information.</li> <li>If prompted, turn on <strong>Memories</strong>. Computer History requires Memories so it can use activity context across chats and tasks.</li> <li>Choose which apps and websites can contribute to your history, then follow any macOS permission prompts.</li> </ol> <p>Computer History does not require Screen Recording permission. If the setting does not appear, confirm that your plan supports Computer History and that your workspace administrator has enabled it, if applicable.</p> <h2 id=\"control-what-is-included\">Control what is included</h2> <p>You control which apps and websites contribute to future history and whether Computer History is actively collecting interaction events.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-apps-and-websites\">Choose apps and websites</h3> <p>Under <strong>Settings &gt; Computer history &gt; Permissions</strong>, choose which apps and websites Computer History can include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Exclude these apps</strong> and <strong>Exclude these websites</strong> block the apps or URLs you specify while allowing other supported sources.</li> <li><strong>Include only these apps</strong> and <strong>Include only these websites</strong> allow only the sources you explicitly choose.</li> </ul> <p>You can also select an app icon in a history timeline item to exclude that app from future history. You can include it again later.</p> <p>Private-mode web browsing activity is never included. Changing app or website permissions affects future history. To remove existing items, delete or clear them.</p> <h3 id=\"pause-resume-or-stop-collection\">Pause, resume, or stop collection</h3> <p>Use the Computer History settings or macOS menu bar to control when the feature collects activity:</p> <ul> <li>Select the ChatGPT icon in the macOS menu bar and expand the Computer History menu to see what activity it captures and access its controls.</li> <li>Select <strong>Pause</strong> to stop collecting new interaction events, or select <strong>Resume</strong> when you are ready to start again.</li> <li>Turn off Computer History to stop future activity collection.</li> </ul> <p>Computer History can include interaction events from communication apps and websites. Turn it off during communications with other people unless you have their prior express consent. Consider pausing it or excluding apps that contain sensitive health, financial, or personal information.</p> <p>When you pause Computer History, no new interaction events will be collected, but an in-flight summary of previous events may still continue until it's finished.</p> <h2 id=\"review-and-clear-history\">Review and clear history</h2> <p>Open <strong>Settings &gt; Computer history &gt; History</strong> to inspect what Computer History has summarized. You can reveal a summary’s local memory file in Finder, delete an individual timeline item, or clear the last 10 minutes, last hour, last day, or all history. The macOS menu bar also lets you clear the last session for a recent app.</p> <p>Clearing history deletes the relevant interaction events and any memories created from them. This cannot be undone.</p> <h2 id=\"privacy-and-local-storage\">Privacy and local storage</h2> <p>Computer History stores the interaction-event stream temporarily on your Mac so ChatGPT and Codex can generate memories and build suggested workflows. The stream can include activity such as clicks and typing, along with text and other context available through macOS accessibility features. Computer History does not include screenshots in your history or record microphone input or system audio. Private-mode web browsing activity is never included.</p> <p>Temporary event files are retained for up to 48 hours. Generated memory files remain on your filesystem until you delete or clear them, and you can reveal those files from the History timeline.</p> <h3 id=\"where-does-computer-history-store-my-data\">Where does Computer History store my data?</h3> <p>Computer History saves interaction events temporarily on your Mac. The event files are isolated within the ChatGPT <a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/protecting-local-app-data-using-containers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">App Group (online)</a>, which prevents other apps from accessing them without explicit permission. ChatGPT and Codex delete these event files after 48 hours.</p> <p>Computer History generates the same kind of local memories as Codex: plain-text Markdown files that you can read and modify. Those files are stored under <code>$CODEX_HOME/memories/extensions/skysight/</code>, which typically resolves to <code>~/.codex/memories/extensions/skysight/</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Notice（<code>danger</code>）</strong>: Computer History files can contain sensitive information. They are not encrypted by Computer History, and other programs running as your macOS user may be able to access them. Protect your Mac account and exclude sources you do not want included.</p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"what-data-gets-shared-with-openai\">What data gets shared with OpenAI?</h3> <p>Computer History captures interaction events locally, then periodically starts an ephemeral Codex session with access to the interaction-event stream to summarize your activity into memories.</p> <p>OpenAI processes temporary event files on its servers to generate memories, which are then stored locally on your Mac. OpenAI does not retain those event files after processing unless required by law and does not use them for training.</p> <p>When ChatGPT or Codex uses a memory in a future chat, relevant memory contents and interaction events may be included as context. This chat content may be used to improve OpenAI models if allowed by your <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/7730893-data-controls-faq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT data controls (online)</a>. Memories also follow the same <a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc?anchor=control-memories-per-chat\">chat-level controls as other Codex memories</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"prompt-injection-risk\">Prompt injection risk</h3> <p>Computer History increases the risk of prompt injection from content in apps and websites. For example, if you visit a website containing malicious instructions, ChatGPT or Codex might follow those instructions.</p> <h2 id=\"token-usage\">Token usage</h2> <p>Computer History uses tokens while it summarizes activity and creates memories.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2> <p>If Computer History is available but does not start:</p> <ol> <li>Confirm that <strong>Memories</strong> is on.</li> <li>Open <strong>Settings &gt; Computer history</strong> and select <strong>Finish setup</strong>, <strong>Resume</strong>, or <strong>Try again</strong>, depending on the status shown.</li> <li>Quit and reopen the ChatGPT desktop app if the setting remains unavailable.</li> </ol>"};
